  "id": "majority-element",
  "questionId": "majority-element",
  "slug": "majority-element",
  "title": "Majority Element",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Hash map",
  "patterns": [
    "hash map"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "the hash map approach is already O(n) time, but it costs O(n) space. since the majority element appears MORE than half the time, is there a way to find it with almost no extra memory?",
    "imagine each occurrence of the majority value as +1 vote and every other value as -1 vote against whatever the current leading candidate is. what happens to the running total over the whole array?",
    "keep a candidate and a count starting at 0. for each number: if count is 0, make it the new candidate; then add 1 to count if the number matches the candidate, or subtract 1 if it doesn't",
    "because the majority element outnumbers everything else combined, it's guaranteed to be the candidate left standing at the end"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "not resetting the candidate when the count hits zero, or resetting at the wrong point in the loop",
    "assuming Boyer-Moore voting works when no true majority exists (it doesn't guarantee a correct answer in that case, but this problem guarantees one exists)",
    "using the hash map approach and calling it done without considering the O(1) space follow-up, missing the point of the pattern"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers `nums`.\n\n**Return the value that appears more than `n/2` times, where `n` is the array's length.**\n\nYou can assume such a value always exists.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 5 * 10^4",
      "-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
      "the majority element always exists in the array"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single element array (it's trivially the majority)",
      "the majority element is exactly n/2 + 1 occurrences",
      "all elements are the same value"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
